//RS 
//RS /// Loading is an unbounded-depth recursive descent over user syntax — the
//RS /// module graph, the parser, and derive/comptime expansion — so the frame
//RS /// requirement is per source-nesting level, not per program size. This is the
//RS /// narrowest point every public `load_entry*` shares, so the sized stack is
//RS /// installed here instead of being chased caller by caller: `Loader::load_entry`
//RS /// and its overlay siblings are public API, and an embedder holding its own
//RS /// entry path — or a 2 MiB libtest worker — would otherwise run the descent on
//RS /// whatever stack it happens to have, aborting the process on overflow.
//RS ///
//RS /// [`crate::run_compiler_work`] is the product boundary rather than
//RS /// `CompilerStack::run_on_compiler_stack` directly, because it owns this
//RS /// crate's thread-local carry: it tests re-entrancy *first*, so an outer
//RS /// boundary (a driver funnel, a JIT public entry) makes this run inline with
//RS /// no capture and no spawn, and on the spawning path it carries the comptime
//RS /// ambient hooks — the one piece of caller-established thread-local state the
//RS /// front end reads — across to the worker.
